menu "Zone source: Z-Wave sensors (zwave_service)"

    config ALARM_ZSRC_ZWAVE
        bool "Zone source: Z-Wave sensors through a Zooz ZAC93"
        default n
        help
            Off-the-shelf Z-Wave door and window contacts, motion, water, smoke, CO and other
            sensors added straight to the panel through a Zooz ZAC93 module on a UART
            (docs/features/36): encrypted with Security 2, supervised by their check-ins, with
            tamper and low battery, working with no Wi-Fi and no Home Assistant. The panel runs
            its own Z-Wave host (components/core/zwave_host) and is its network's only
            controller.

            Needs PSRAM: the network's state is about 160 KB. The radio stays off until a place
            is chosen (`zwave place socket|j7` on the console, or the Flasher): until then no
            pin is touched. Every board's manifest states this option: the CrowPanel P4's turns
            it on (docs/features/36 Z9); a board without PSRAM leaves it off.

    if ALARM_ZSRC_ZWAVE
    config ALARM_ZWAVE_S0
        bool "Allow the older S0 security (phase 3, not built yet)"
        default n
        help
            Reserved for docs/features/36 phase 3 (security.md §10): devices that only speak S0.
            The host grants no S0 key in this firmware whatever this says.

    config ALARM_ZWAVE_LR
        bool "Z-Wave Long Range (phase 3, not built yet)"
        default n
        help
            Reserved for docs/features/36 phase 3 (network.md §13): 16-bit node IDs and the Long
            Range node list at start-up where the region has it. Off: classic Z-Wave only.

    config ALARM_ZWAVE_UART_NUM
        int "UART controller for the ZAC93"
        range 1 4
        default 3
        help
            UART0 is the service console and UART2 the ESP32-H2 sensor radio's
            (docs/features/20); the ZAC93 takes UART3 (docs/features/36 hardware.md §4).
    endif

endmenu
